From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the yy_fatal_error() workaround

flex 2.6.5 renamed the generated scanner's yy_fatal_error() to yypanic(),
so the dead-code call kept only to silence -Wunused-function no longer
compiles. do_fatal_error() is used by YY_FATAL_ERROR(), so drop the hack.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-12
---
 connectivity/source/parse/sqlflex.l | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/connectivity/source/parse/sqlflex.l b/connectivity/source/parse/sqlflex.l
--- a/connectivity/source/parse/sqlflex.l
+++ b/connectivity/source/parse/sqlflex.l
@@ -96,12 +96,10 @@
 // coverity[+kill]
 static void do_fatal_error(const char* msg)
 {
     xxx_pGLOBAL_SQLSCAN->SQLyyerror(msg);
-    /*hack to silence -Wunused-function*/
-    if ((0)) yy_fatal_error(msg);
 }
 
 #define YY_FATAL_ERROR(msg) \
 {                           \
     do_fatal_error(msg);    \
 }
